#! /bin/bash

######################################################################
############## Begin Script Information Block ########################
######################################################################
# Name: postinstall
# Author: Heath Jones
# Date: 2026-06-13
# Modified: 2026-09-26
# Purpose: Serberus PKG postinstall — check the PAM module's directory chain
#          (before touching the module), run the 10-criterion upgrade
#          validation, write version.plist, bootstrap the LaunchDaemon, wait
#          until it is actually UP (one pid for 8 s with no launchd restart, a
#          state.plist written by THIS daemon, healthy `serberus status`),
#          re-check the pid, then line-merge sudo_local. The break-glass preflight
#          runs in the PREINSTALL, before the upgrade teardown.
#          Every failure — including an unexpected `set -e` exit, via the
#          EXIT trap — takes the same abort path: remove the sudoers drop-in,
#          unwire sudo_local (if either survives, the daemon is kept enabled
#          and running and the script exits 1 loudly), then disable the
#          daemon, boot it out and wait until launchd has dropped it, re-check
#          the drop-in, demote JIT admins, restore the AuthorizationDB (never
#          by executing a daemon that failed signature validation, and never
#          beside a daemon that is still loaded), and write state=degraded
#          with the real reason. Installer output, this script's included,
#          is in /var/log/install.log.
# Version: 1.8 - (a) The serberus CLI's folder chain (/usr/local/bin,
#          /usr/local, /usr) is checked up front: when it is not root-only the
#          install aborts with that reason (it used to abort later as "never
#          came up"), and the payload CLI is removed from the user-writable
#          folder. (b) The abort path waits the daemon's ExitTimeOut plus 5 s
#          after the bootout. (c) The first log line says where the installer
#          log is. (d) The header states the abort order the script follows.
#          (e) version.plist records execGate (enabled | disabled) from the
#          EXEC_GATE file build-pkg.sh stages; an ESF=off build is disabled.
#          1.7 - (a) The component versions come from the VERSION file
#          build-pkg.sh stages beside this script (the repository's single
#          version source). (b) version.plist records installTeamID, the
#          Team ID the daemon was validated against; teardowns pin the daemon
#          to it. (c) A stray /usr/local/lib/pam/pam_serberus.so.2 (OpenPAM
#          loads it in place of pam_serberus.so) is removed before sudo_local
#          is wired; one that cannot be removed aborts the install. (d) The
#          abort path disables the daemon after sudo_local is unwired, just
#          before the bootout, so an interrupted abort never leaves a wired
#          sudo_local behind a disabled daemon. (e) After the bootout the abort
#          path waits (up to the 20 s ExitTimeOut) for launchd to drop the
#          job; if it is still loaded the one-shots are skipped and the manual
#          steps logged.
#          1.6 - (a) "Up" is stricter: the bootstrap time is recorded first
#          and the daemon must write a state.plist (not `unknown`) no older
#          than it; one pid must hold for 8 s (past the 5 s ThrottleInterval)
#          with launchd's `runs` unchanged and no failed exit recorded; the
#          pid is re-read right before sudo_local is merged. (b) Criterion
#          10: the serberus CLI is present, mode 755, root-owned and signed
#          by the daemon's team; a missing CLI fails the health check. (c)
#          The daemon is trusted for execution only through
#          serberus_daemon_trusted (strict signature, Apple anchor, identifier
#          com.herojoneslabs.serberus.daemon, its team). (d) A sudoers
#          drop-in that survives its removal stops the abort path BEFORE
#          sudo_local is unwired, with the daemon kept running. (e) A chown
#          failure on sudo_local is no longer hidden by the chmod after it.
#          (f) --demote-jit exit 3 (no grant store) is informational.
#          (g) Version 0.9.0.
#          1.5 - (a) EXIT trap right after pam-lib.sh is sourced: any
#          unexpected exit before the success marker runs abort_install.
#          (b) The abort keeps the daemon enabled and running (and exits 1
#          loudly) when an active pam_serberus line survives the unwire. (c)
#          "Up" = the same pid for ~3 s AND a healthy `serberus status`
#          (pam-lib serberus_launchd_wait_running). (d) umask 022. (e) The
#          module's directory chain is checked BEFORE any chown/chmod, and the
#          module is locked with chown -h / chmod -h (symlinks refused). (f)
#          A daemon that failed signature validation is never executed for
#          --demote-jit / --restore-authdb; manual instructions are printed
#          instead. One-shots are bounded (120 s; a timeout is a loud
#          failure). (g) state.plist records the real degraded reason
#          (pam_not_wired / auth_plugin_unavailable), not a fixed
#          config_invalid. (h) The break-glass preflight moved to the
#          preinstall (it ran here only after the upgrade teardown). (i) Warns
#          loudly when /etc/pam.d/sudo does not include sudo_local as its
#          first auth line (never edits it). (j) Locks down the installed
#          uninstall.sh + pam-lib.sh under the support dir.
#          1.4 - (a) Refuses a target volume other than "/" ($3). (b) Tools
#          by absolute path (no `which` under root). (c) The PAM module and
#          the SerberusAuth plugin must be signed by the SAME team as the
#          installed daemon (codesign -R), and the daemon must carry a Team
#          ID at all. (d) The module's directory chain (/usr … the module)
#          must be root-owned and not group/other-writable before
#          sudo_local is wired. (e) "Daemon up" now means a running pid
#          within ~10 s of bootstrap, not merely a loaded job (an AMFI kill
#          loop stays loaded). (f) `launchctl enable` before bootstrap so a
#          label disabled by an earlier uninstall/abort cannot block the
#          install. (g) Every abort path disables + boots out the daemon,
#          removes the sudoers drop-in, unwires sudo_local, demotes JIT
#          admins and restores the AuthorizationDB, so a reboot can never
#          resurrect an ungated daemon. (h) Ships and validates the
#          SerberusAuth authorization plugin.
#          1.3 - (a) PATH no longer includes /usr/local/bin: a user who owns
#          it could otherwise plant tools this root script runs. (b) The
#          PAM module arch check uses file(1), not lipo, which exists only
#          with the Command Line Tools and made the check fail on endpoints.
#          (c) The abort path removes the coarse sudoers drop-in before
#          unwiring sudo_local, so a failed install never leaves the
#          path-only drop-in without the PAM gate behind it.
#          1.2 - (a) PAM module relocated to /usr/local/lib/pam/
#          pam_serberus.so — /usr/lib/pam sits on the SEALED read-only APFS
#          system snapshot (macOS 11+) and can never hold a third-party
#          module; sudo_local references it by ABSOLUTE path via pam-lib.sh.
#          (b) Every abort path now UNWIRES a sudo_local left wired by a
#          previous install (marker-aware) — the preinstall has already
#          booted the daemon out and the old binary may already be replaced,
#          so exiting with a wired sudo_local and no daemon would hard-deny
#          every sudo. (c) Upgrade validation gains a native-arch criterion
#          (lipo) mirroring the test pkg. (d) Break-glass preflight now
#          requires a RESOLVABLE pamBypass user/group (typo'd entries provide
#          zero bypass).
#          1.1 - create_sudo_local_if_absent replaced with the shared
#          pam-lib.sh line-merge (idempotent; Serberus line inserted ABOVE any
#          pre-existing `auth sufficient pam_tid.so` so Touch ID cannot bypass
#          Serberus; user lines never clobbered; from-scratch content comes
#          from the staged Support/sudo_local — single source of truth). Adds
#          the break-glass preflight: ABORTS before wiring sudo_local when the
#          effective com.herojoneslabs.serberus.config is enforce-or-absent
#          with an empty pamBypass — pam_serberus fails closed and would brick
#          sudo for everyone. Fails closed against installation only; never
#          modifies sudo config on failure.
#          1.0 - Initial Script
#
######################################################################
############## End Script Information Block ##########################
######################################################################

